1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,500
Little Moments.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,302
The Missing Water Bottle.

3
00:00:03,302 --> 00:00:07,094
After gym class, I reach into the side pocket of my backpack.

4
00:00:07,094 --> 00:00:08,698
No water bottle.

5
00:00:08,698 --> 00:00:11,958
I check the other side, even though it has never lived there.

6
00:00:11,958 --> 00:00:13,479
Still nothing.

7
00:00:13,706 --> 00:00:15,041
When did you last have it?

8
00:00:15,316 --> 00:00:16,924
Before basketball.

9
00:00:16,924 --> 00:00:18,924
I think I left it in the gym.

10
00:00:18,924 --> 00:00:21,456
We go back, but the bench is empty.

11
00:00:21,456 --> 00:00:25,591
Emma suggests checking the school office, where there's a box for lost things.

12
00:00:25,876 --> 00:00:27,408
Looking for something?

13
00:00:27,628 --> 00:00:29,143
My water bottle.

14
00:00:29,143 --> 00:00:31,684
I had it this morning, and now it's missing.

15
00:00:31,972 --> 00:00:33,599
What does it look like?

16
00:00:33,820 --> 00:00:36,022
It's dark blue with a silver lid.

17
00:00:36,022 --> 00:00:39,657
There's a little moon sticker on one side and a scratch near the bottom.

18
00:00:39,940 --> 00:00:41,194
Let's see.

19
00:00:41,194 --> 00:00:43,340
We have two blue bottles here.

20
00:00:43,340 --> 00:00:45,402
Does either of these look familiar?

21
00:00:45,676 --> 00:00:47,597
The first one has a red lid.

22
00:00:47,597 --> 00:00:51,076
The second has my little moon, slightly peeling at one corner.

23
00:00:51,076 --> 00:00:52,482
That's the one!

24
00:00:52,706 --> 00:00:54,000
Your moon brought you home.

25
00:00:54,268 --> 00:00:56,062
Is your name on it anywhere?

26
00:00:56,284 --> 00:00:57,496
Not yet.

27
00:00:57,496 --> 00:00:59,486
I should probably fix that.

28
00:00:59,764 --> 00:01:02,943
A name label would make it easier to return next time.

29
00:01:03,172 --> 00:01:06,874
At home, I dry the bottle and add a small label under the moon.

30
00:01:06,874 --> 00:01:09,957
Ben offers to write an exciting name instead of Lucy.

31
00:01:09,957 --> 00:01:12,634
Later, I tell Emma about it on the phone.

32
00:01:12,866 --> 00:01:13,660
Like what?

33
00:01:13,948 --> 00:01:15,556
Captain Splash.

34
00:01:15,556 --> 00:01:18,702
I decide Lucy is more useful for the school office.

35
00:01:18,702 --> 00:01:23,390
Captain Splash can be its name at home, where nobody needs to fill out a lost-and-found form.
